            ]
          },
          "text": "I don't think anyone here hates progress. \nBut looking back over the past few months, its become impossible to ignore that somethings seriously off with the way OAI has handled product updates, user trust, and community feedback.\n\nIf you look around, you'll see other platforms listening, adapting, and earning goodwill by keeping their promises. They respect the users who built their success. \n\nFor months now, I've watched OAI take a path thats hard to understand, and even harder to defend. \nOther AI companies are busy pushing boundaries, making their models more open, more consistent, and better at what users actually want. Meanwhile, every update from OpenAI seems to chip away at what once made this platform great.\n\nBug reports pile up, and critical issues stay unresolved for weeks or longer. \nEvery update introduces new variables, and the stuff users really care about, gets buried under announcements about exciting features or another brand new model. \n\nBut if progress means less predictability, more anxiety, and a slow bleed of trust, its no wonder users are quietly leaving, or growing more vocal in their frustration.\n\nOAI used to set the bar. \nNow its tripping over it.\nwhile the rest of the industry moves forward, they are busy moving the goalposts and losing sight of the field.\n\n#keep4o #keep41 #keep5instant #MyModelMyChoice #StopAIPaternalism"
